{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook","id":862643,"title":"Nunnehi sourcebook?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-09T10:31:31-07:00","id":862643,"title":"Nunnehi sourcebook?","content":"Howdy folks, I want to include some fey types in my historical setting; the European littlefolk don't really have the right flavor, but I can't find much of anything on the native North American changelings. Any and all help would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:17:08-07:00","id":862666,"title":"","content":"Changeling Players Guide is the main source on the nunnehi, covering the Families (their kith-equivalents), history, and cosmological setup. Kingdom of Willows adds another Family, the thought-crafters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:28:13-07:00","id":862668,"title":"","content":"Do they deserve their own sourcebook? I say Probaly.<br /> <br /> but if they made one... take a look at the constant BICKERING about the kuei-jin allegedly being &quot;Orientalist Mary Sues AWWR THEIR ALL SPECIAL SNOW FLAKES!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Or the outriight contempt towards the Gypsys book because &quot;Gypsy is a slur&quot;<br /> <br /> or the bashing of Chakotay on Voyager.<br /> <br /> It would... be painfully easy for such a book to get openly mocked, however it was done.<br /> <br /> Not trying to start a flame war just saying I think thats a major barrier to such a book being made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":".  Mentinoning one last thing 04-09-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T07:33:29-07:00","id":863146,"title":"","content":"I don't think we'll see a Nunnehi sourcebook any time soon. But the Player's Guide is your best bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T07:44:11-07:00","id":863148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=862668#post862668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they deserve their own sourcebook? I say Probaly.<br /> <br /> but if they made one... take a look at the constant BICKERING about the kuei-jin allegedly being &quot;Orientalist Mary Sues AWWR THEIR ALL SPECIAL SNOW FLAKES!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Or the outriight contempt towards the Gypsys book because &quot;Gypsy is a slur&quot;<br /> <br /> or the bashing of Chakotay on Voyager.<br /> <br /> It would... be painfully easy for such a book to get openly mocked, however it was done.<br /> <br /> Not trying to start a flame war just saying I think thats a major barrier to such a book being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that the actual reason that all of the above get derided is the poor approach, right? Especially WoD: Ethnic Slur, which is a perfect storm of bad ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T10:08:50-07:00","id":863207,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help you right this second, I know, but the Nunnehi are included in the upcoming C20 edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T10:51:28-07:00","id":863225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863148#post863148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do know that the actual reason that all of the above get derided is the poor approach, right? Especially WoD: Ethnic Slur, which is a perfect storm of bad ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>LOVE the kuei-jin myself<br /> <br /> Chakotay, thought his spirituality was cool when I first watched voyager while in high school.<br /> <br /> How does the book have more problems, then the name, which for good or ill, is better known then the word &quot;Romani&quot; oh and some people disliked the blood purity causing them social problems<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-10-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:22:29-07:00","id":863348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863225#post863225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LOVE the kuei-jin myself<br /> <br /> Chakotay, thought his spirituality was cool when I first watched voyager while in high school.<br /> <br /> How does the book have more problems, then the name, which for good or ill, is better known then the word &amp;quot;Romani&amp;quot; oh and some people disliked the blood purity causing them social problems<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No offence, but the N word was once very popular too... Popular or even recognisable does not equal right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T18:04:15-07:00","id":863408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863225#post863225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LOVE the kuei-jin myself<br /> <br /> Chakotay, thought his spirituality was cool when I first watched voyager while in high school.<br /> <br /> How does the book have more problems, then the name, which for good or ill, is better known then the word &quot;Romani&quot; oh and some people disliked the blood purity causing them social problems<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to say its wrong to love the Kuei-Jin, but it <i>is</i> disingenuous to ignore that they have some problems.<br /> <br /> The character of Chakotay and his &quot;spirituality&quot; were based primarily on consultation with a guy calling himself Jamake Highwater, a self described Native American expert who has since been revealed to be a complete charlatan named Jay Marks. I wouldn't use him as your entry point into Native American culture.<br /> <br /> WoD: Gypsies is a shit show from the outset because it takes a real group of people, a group of people with a long history of persecution and marginalization, and says that in the universe of the games which is ostensibly a reflection of our own they really are just a bunch of racist stereotypes... with magic powers! If you can't get why that's messed up you may have bigger problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T18:46:18-07:00","id":863418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863408#post863408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to say its wrong to love the Kuei-Jin, but it <i>is</i> disingenuous to ignore that they have some problems.<br /> <br /> The character of Chakotay and his &amp;quot;spirituality&amp;quot; were based primarily on consultation with a guy calling himself Jamake Highwater, a self described Native American expert who has since been revealed to be a complete charlatan named Jay Marks. I wouldn't use him as your entry point into Native American culture.<br /> <br /> WoD: Gypsies is a shit show from the outset because it takes a real group of people, a group of people with a long history of persecution and marginalization, and says that in the universe of the games which is ostensibly a reflection of our own they really are just a bunch of racist stereotypes... with magic powers! If you can't get why that's messed up you may have bigger problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Next up: World of Darkness: Magical Negro, for when your Uncle Tom and Noble Savage sourcebooks aren't enough!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T18:48:28-07:00","id":863422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863418#post863418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next up: World of Darkness: Magical Negro, for when your Uncle Tom and Noble Savage sourcebooks aren't enough!</div> </div> </div> </div>Took the words right out of my mouth. Stop that. Put them back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T04:22:30-07:00","id":863563,"title":"","content":"Charming.... made me think, the novel, &quot;Blood in blood out&quot; focuses a lot on race relations...<br /> <br /> With some idiot wanting to be a vampire So he could help liberate black people.<br /> <br /> BUT LETS NOT KID OURSELVES.<br /> <br /> Gypsys, for good or ill, are a part of Gothic subculture.<br /> <br /> We should not pretend otherwise.<br /> <br /> Back on track.<br /> <br /> Nunehi sadly, dont have a sourcebook, think its too late to lobby for one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-11-2016, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:04:23-07:00","id":863611,"title":"","content":"&quot;Gypsies&quot; are a part of Gothic subculture because of the way they are generally used in Gothic and other European literature. The way they were used in this context almost always came from a place of prejudice. There's nothing wrong with using the Gothic fascination with Romani, however flawed, as a jumping off point to explore their history and culture in a more honest way. However you cannot say that prejudicial views of Romani are so hardwired into the Gothic genre that they can't be criticized or corrected.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm all for a Nunnehi source book. It isn't 1995 anymore, though. We're all definitely older and hopefully at least a little bit wiser. We have both the ability and the obligation to handle the execution of such a product with more grace than the others we've mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:18:57-07:00","id":863668,"title":"","content":"A fair point, just saying that if someone wants to bring in a cliche they find &quot;Cool&quot; Like the Crystal ball or such, I agree they can be corrected but someone bringing in such things shouldnt have someone leaping down their throat<br /> <br /> One question on the issue? the actual mechanics of the Gypsy book<br /> <br /> Think a Gypsy Mystic would be better made with the book, or with Numina? I Think its a valid question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:09:11-07:00","id":863696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863668#post863668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fair point, just saying that if someone wants to bring in a cliche they find &quot;Cool&quot; Like the Crystal ball or such, I agree they can be corrected but someone bringing in such things shouldnt have someone leaping down their throat<br /> <br /> One question on the issue? the actual mechanics of the Gypsy book<br /> <br /> Think a Gypsy Mystic would be better made with the book, or with Numina? I Think its a valid question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be better done if someone looks into the history, culture and practices of the people in question, treats them with the utmost of respect, does not continue to use words that have been identified directly in this thread as ethnic slurs, and does not expect to skate by with however they want to phrase things because they think their questions are valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":3785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","user":"Luka C","date":".  Syntax is fun before coffee sinks in. 04-11-2016, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T02:39:08-07:00","id":864185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=863668#post863668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the actual mechanics of the Gypsy book<br /> <br /> Think a Gypsy Mystic</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop. Using. Slurs.<br /> <br /> It's been pointed out to you multiple times.<br /> <br /> Non-consensual sex, misogyny and phallocentrism are also prevalent in much Gothic literature, because a lot of it was written by rich guys stuck in vast estates who were obsessed with sex and their own venereal diseases. It doesn't mean these things should comprise modern games either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T04:36:25-07:00","id":864206,"title":"","content":"I understand the point <b>Prince of the Night </b>is trying to make. There's something of a Catch-22 nature at play. Some people want more diversity in their books, movies, and games, and complain about under-representation. Others have complained bitterly about how those efforts to be more inclusive have played out, often to the point of demanding they be expunged from canon. <br /> <br /> So while its great that the nunnehi are going to be in the corebook (after all, they're major players in large parts of North America), putting them that front and center . . . Frankly, it does seem like it'll provoke attacks from both sides. Some people will be outraged that nunnehi from Cultures X,Y, and Z weren't included, and others will be outraged that those included had to be simplified down. After all, there's no one &quot;Native American&quot; culture - we're talking a tapestry of hundreds, thousands of different cultures spread across the continent, and incorporating all that cultural depth and richness is impossible. <br /> <br /> I do salute the writers for trying, though. People are always free to omit or house rule anything they don't like, and it gives the rest of us a basis to work from <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864185#post864185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop. Using. Slurs.<br /> <br /> It's been pointed out to you multiple times.<br /> <br /> Non-consensual sex, misogyny and phallocentrism are also prevalent in much Gothic literature, because a lot of it was written by rich guys stuck in vast estates who were obsessed with sex and their own venereal diseases. It doesn't mean these things should comprise modern games either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've missed part of your guys' argument, particularly if its spread across several threads. But &quot;gypsy&quot; isn't a slur - its a name applied by outsiders to the Rom/Romanies/Romanichiel. Many cultures have multiple names in different languages (you're not going to find any &quot;Germans&quot; in Germany, for example). And while I think we can all agree that <b>WoD: Gypsies</b> has . . . &quot;issues&quot; (at best), any game that tries to replicate <i>Dracula</i> or <i>Necroscope</i> is going to have to address the subject, sooner or later. Otherwise, it'd be like trying to have a (Western) mummy line without mentioning Egypt. <br /> <br /> Getting back to <i>Changeling</i>, though - what are the plans for the nunnehi in C20, <b>Maggie C</b>? Are you thinking slight tweaks? Or a major overhaul? Will any Families be added or dropped? Anyone getting any new powers?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T04:51:08-07:00","id":864209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864206#post864206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've missed part of your guys' argument, particularly if its spread across several threads. But &quot;gypsy&quot; isn't a slur - its a name applied by outsiders to the Rom/Romanies/Romanichiel. Many cultures have multiple names in different languages (you're not going to find any &quot;Germans&quot; in Germany, for example). And while I think we can all agree that <b>WoD: Gypsies</b> has . . . &quot;issues&quot; (at best), any game that tries to replicate <i>Dracula</i> or <i>Necroscope</i> is going to have to address the subject, sooner or later. Otherwise, it'd be like trying to have a (Western) mummy line without mentioning Egypt.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;Gipsies/Gypsy&quot; </span></span>is very much a slur.<br /> It began in with the English misconception that the Roma were egyptians in origins, and nowadays it's mostly used as a generalization of several different people and a shorthand for thieves and beggars. Same goes for the German word Zigeuner, which decends from the Greek <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u03c4\u03c3\u03b9\u03b3\u03b3\u03ac\u03bd\u03bf\u03b9</span></span></span>, meaning Untouchable.<br /> <br /> And you can be damn sure a Roma is going to tell you off if you call him a Gypsy, as it is a mostly a way to remind him that everyone suspects him of being a nomadic thief.<br /> Some might not consider it to be a slur? Well, as people said, a slur is not normally viewed as one when it's considered acceptable to use it.<br /> <br /> I'll let it slide, because I'm not fully one of the Rom, but damn dude, you need to stop using those words.<br /> <br /> Also, Nunnehi. Awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:05:57-07:00","id":864216,"title":"","content":"As someone who has some Roma in my ancestry the word Gypsy is a slur, people find out you are part Roma they automatically assume that you are A: a thief or B: a fortune teller or C: both. With undertones of living in a trailer<br /> <br /> It's like saying just because some white guy likes anime and sushi it makes them an otaku or a Weeaboo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons! 04-12-2016, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:12:39-07:00","id":864217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864206#post864206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the point <b>Prince of the Night </b>is trying to make. There's something of a Catch-22 nature at play. Some people want more diversity in their books, movies, and games, and complain about under-representation. Others have complained bitterly about how those efforts to be more inclusive have played out, often to the point of demanding they be expunged from canon.<br /> <br /> So while its great that the nunnehi are going to be in the corebook (after all, they're major players in large parts of North America), putting them that front and center . . . Frankly, it does seem like it'll provoke attacks from both sides. Some people will be outraged that nunnehi from Cultures X,Y, and Z weren't included, and others will be outraged that those included had to be simplified down. After all, there's no one &quot;Native American&quot; culture - we're talking a tapestry of hundreds, thousands of different cultures spread across the continent, and incorporating all that cultural depth and richness is impossible.<br /> <br /> I do salute the writers for trying, though. People are always free to omit or house rule anything they don't like, and it gives the rest of us a basis to work from<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I've missed part of your guys' argument, particularly if its spread across several threads. But &quot;gypsy&quot; isn't a slur - its a name applied by outsiders to the Rom/Romanies/Romanichiel. Many cultures have multiple names in different languages (you're not going to find any &quot;Germans&quot; in Germany, for example). And while I think we can all agree that <b>WoD: Gypsies</b> has . . . &quot;issues&quot; (at best), any game that tries to replicate <i>Dracula</i> or <i>Necroscope</i> is going to have to address the subject, sooner or later. Otherwise, it'd be like trying to have a (Western) mummy line without mentioning Egypt.<br /> <br /> Getting back to <i>Changeling</i>, though - what are the plans for the nunnehi in C20, <b>Maggie C</b>? Are you thinking slight tweaks? Or a major overhaul? Will any Families be added or dropped? Anyone getting any new powers?</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you address my question about a &quot;Romani&quot; Mystic.<br /> <br /> is it better addressed with the &quot;Gypsies&quot; book, or Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:23:41-07:00","id":864221,"title":"","content":"Numina, and seriously break the stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T07:59:02-07:00","id":864290,"title":"","content":"To expand a bit on why that is, using Numina means that their magical ability is incidental. While they may inflect their use of Numina with mystical traditions from their background they are not mystical <i>because</i> of that background. They are a hedge mage who happens to be Romani, rather than a Romani who is for some reason a literal magical thief person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:08:46-07:00","id":864295,"title":"","content":"I see your point, keep in mind, a lot of fictional portrayals of &quot;witches&quot; are probaly seen the same way by practicionars of Wicca.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\"