ot; Attire, if they think it makes them look cool, or if their Reading someones fortune for money at a circus or whatever, Is likely NOT Romani by blood, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they want to be ass-hats that's their business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:11:28-07:00","id":864371,"title":"","content":"On topic though (both of them really), there is at least one other book I know of with information on the Nunnehi, though I hesitate to suggest it.<br /> <br /> Rage Across Appalachia has a chapter on the Nunnehi, and if you could just take material from there while ignoring the rest of the book that would probably be for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:55:58-07:00","id":864460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=862668#post862668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they deserve their own sourcebook? I say Probaly.<br /> <br /> but if they made one... take a look at the constant BICKERING about the kuei-jin allegedly being &quot;Orientalist Mary Sues AWWR THEIR ALL SPECIAL SNOW FLAKES!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Or the outriight contempt towards the Gypsys book because &quot;Gypsy is a slur&quot;<br /> <br /> or the bashing of Chakotay on Voyager.<br /> <br /> It would... be painfully easy for such a book to get openly mocked, however it was done.<br /> <br /> Not trying to start a flame war just saying I think thats a major barrier to such a book being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still vote for a Sourcebook to detail the Nunnehi and the Menehine to get a sourcebook. These character types need, and deserve the detail that could be added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:03:09-07:00","id":864468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864216#post864216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who has some Roma in my ancestry the word Gypsy is a slur, people find out you are part Roma they automatically assume that you are A: a thief or B: a fortune teller or C: both. With undertones of living in a trailer<br /> <br /> It's like saying just because some white guy likes anime and sushi it makes them an otaku or a Weeaboo.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Ouspenskaya\" target=\"_blank\">this woman's</a> performance as Maleva is so overwhelming powerful that the idea or image of the &quot;Gypsy&quot; can't be removed from the type of fiction we're playing with here. What was needed was a book that handled the real world origins of the fictional archetype and offered ways for players to use PCs and NPCs based on the Roma. Maleva is still far to cool to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:49:19-07:00","id":864501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864468#post864468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Ouspenskaya\" target=\"_blank\">this woman's</a> performance as Maleva is so overwhelming powerful that the idea or image of the &amp;quot;Gypsy&amp;quot; can't be removed from the type of fiction we're playing with here. What was needed was a book that handled the real world origins of the fictional archetype and offered ways for players to use PCs and NPCs based on the Roma. Maleva is still far to cool to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>James Baskett was awesome in song of the south, can I have my magical Negro book now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:01:10-07:00","id":864510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864468#post864468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Ouspenskaya\" target=\"_blank\">this woman's</a> performance as Maleva is so overwhelming powerful that the idea or image of the &quot;Gypsy&quot; can't be removed from the type of fiction we're playing with here. What was needed was a book that handled the real world origins of the fictional archetype and offered ways for players to use PCs and NPCs based on the Roma. Maleva is still far to cool to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But you can still call her a &quot;Romani Fortuneteller&quot; without using the word that keeps insisting that my grandfather was a part of a pack of thieves when he escaped KZ-camps and then worked his entire life as a postal worker, still being harassed by people calling him a thieving gypsy.<br /> Seriously, it's not hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:36:13-07:00","id":864537,"title":"","content":"Yes thing is, Romani refers to the &quot;Real&quot; group in the real world<br /> <br /> &quot;Gypsy&quot; References the Romani, as well as fictional groups like Ravenlofts Vistani.<br /> <br /> Also Gypsy also Adds a degree of mysticism to the connotations.<br /> <br /> Im sorry your grandfather got harassed really.<br /> <br /> Im of german ancestory should I take offense when people speak down about Germany? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop