flame war, was pointing all of this out, to warn of the obstacles to a nunehi sourcebook, sad though it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T16:55:18-07:00","id":864614,"title":"","content":"Yes language does evolve, just like how someone used be called a asianphile we now call a Weeaboo. Does that still make it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:22:52-07:00","id":864957,"title":"","content":"Consulting my shelf I did find one other book with information on the Nunnehi. The Shining Host Players Guide for LARP. What I don't know is how much overlap that information has with the tabletop Players Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:45:15-07:00","id":865300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864371#post864371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On topic though (both of them really), there is at least one other book I know of with information on the Nunnehi, though I hesitate to suggest it.<br /> <br /> Rage Across Appalachia has a chapter on the Nunnehi, and if you could just take material from there while ignoring the rest of the book that would probably be for the best.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Them's fighting Words the Amish Get of Fenris is a work of art! The one Kitsune who randomly fucks with fox hunts for no reason also ART!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T21:38:00-07:00","id":865321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=865300#post865300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Them's fighting Words the Amish Get of Fenris is a work of art! The one Kitsune who randomly fucks with fox hunts for no reason also ART!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's early Werewolf. The subtitle might as well have been &quot;A game of condescending paternalism.&quot;<br /> <br /> I legitimately wouldn't mind a new W20 Rage Across Appalachia. Just hopefully one that isn't, you know, completely full of shit. We could even be really crazy and get some actual people from Appalachia in on it. I imagine the end result wouldn't be nearly as marketable though, with its manifest lack of exploitable hillbilly tropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T00:11:24-07:00","id":865354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864611#post864611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but language evolves. Thats the point im making<br /> <br /> And made it clear I DIDNT want to start a flame war, was pointing all of this out, to warn of the obstacles to a nunehi sourcebook, sad though it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that make it okay to, say, call you a douche because it's cool or hip?<br /> <br /> Please just stop using slurs and claiming like you should be allowed to just because you want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:09:37-07:00","id":865405,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Prince of the Night, it's been pointed out repeatedly that Gypsy is considered a slur and it is not acceptable for use on these forums. It's unfortunate there was a book titled that back in the 90's, the company took it as a learning experience. Use the opportunity I'm giving you now to treat this as a learning experience and stop using the term, or your posting privileges will be suspended.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:24:58-07:00","id":865463,"title":"","content":"Arguing with a Mod is an inherently bad idea, I just came in here wanting to tell him Why I didnt think a Nunehi sourcebook would be workable then alas I got into (yet another) Argument on that book.<br /> <br /> I Have no case to make save for a plea to beware the proliferation of political correctness, and I think that case has allready been noted, and rejected. I will not endlessly remake it in slightly different fashions, it is beneath my dignity.<br /> <br /> So I will ride off nobly into the sunset, never to return to this thread, until the setting of the last sun. I will try to avoid this topic alltogether if I can, but will not vouchsafe the word will not accidently come into play, as I was taught it as common use english for decades. :Gallops away speedily:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:19:43-07:00","id":865511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=865463#post865463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I will try to avoid this topic alltogether if I can, but will not vouchsafe the word will not accidently come into play, as I was taught it as common use english for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... rest in pepperonis?<br /> I won't bother pointing out the obvious parallels between this line of thinking and defending the N-word, because you left the thread.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I figure a full Nunnehi sourcebook would be awesome. There are lots of weird and wacky 'little folk' like creatures in Native American folklore. I hope such a topic isn't such a minefield that any future developments would be impossible... including more Indigenous material would be really nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T04:50:16-07:00","id":867488,"title":"","content":"On topic.<br /> <br /> I'd say there's a fine line to walk with Native American folklore. Any misconceptions has to be either rooted out or used as what they are: misconceptions.<br /> You can do a lot with the current research, but Nunnehi should be as diverse as the European faes, perhaps even more so.<br /> The southern Nunnehi from the deserts of Mexico should not have anything in common with the orca-swimming Nunnehi of the Pacific Northwest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:08:01-07:00","id":903827,"title":"","content":"If the Nunnehi get a sourcebook (as they should), i would like the emphasis on the fact that they are not &quot;Fairies&quot;.<br /> I like the idea of Kithain getting to America to find these guys with a link to the Dreaming, and powers similar enough to their own that the ignorant Werewolves and Mages get away with calling Fae... but different enough that even though a couple centuries have come and gone since that first meeting, they are still considered Gallain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:11:44-07:00","id":903901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luisarmander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=903827#post903827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Nunnehi get a sourcebook (as they should), i would like the emphasis on the fact that they are not &quot;Fairies&quot;.<br /> I like the idea of Kithain getting to America to find these guys with a link to the Dreaming, and powers similar enough to their own that the ignorant Werewolves and Mages get away with calling Fae... but different enough that even though a couple centuries have come and gone since that first meeting, they are still considered Gallain</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What makes something a Fairy? What makes something a creature of the Dreaming vs the Umbra? I think its very interesting Eshu have become Kithain while Nunnehi remain on the outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:22:43-07:00","id":904352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=903901#post903901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What makes something a Fairy? What makes something a creature of the Dreaming vs the Umbra? I think its very interesting Eshu have become Kithain while Nunnehi remain on the outside.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cynical part of me thinks it's because African-Americans are more vocal and have more buying power in the US than Native Americans, particularly at the time CTD was first published. TV and film, for instance, do at least pretend to include black people, but Native American actors and characters are far, far less visible.<br /> <br /> Within the game itself, that probably also translates to the World of Darkness. The fae aren't accurate representations of nuanced folkloric beliefs, but rather broad archetypes based on cultural tropes. <br /> <br /> The Eshu, then, represent popular conceptions of the dreams and folklore of the African Diaspora in the US, which is closer to popular understanding than Native American traditions. Black power, civil rights, Afrocentrism and black music in general have all made Black consciousness a (small but significant) part of American culture.<br /> <br /> Indeed, you could even argue that the way the Eshu actually conflate several different cultures and their folklore is because American Black politics (with a capital B) actually merges widely disparate cultures into one African-American identity.<br /> <br /> Native American beliefs, being more closely guarded, retaining (in some cases) their distinctiveness to a greater degree, without the homogenisation African-American culture has faced, and being less 'popular'/well known in general therefore aren't archetypal or broad enough to cluster into kiths. What we end up with is part-spirit beings who are the remnants of more hyperlocal traditions, who've resisted being subsumed into a more uniform kithain identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-31-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:29:34-07:00","id":904358,"title":"","content":"Also, as a case in point, the Eshu kith throws in Asian tropes, despite being named after a West African god (West Africa being the origin of most African-Americans who arrived via the slave trase).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T07:14:36-07:00","id":1097114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=864501#post864501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> James Baskett was awesome in song of the south, can I have my magical Negro book now?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that the two subjects are profoundly different. Maria Ouspenskaya performance was meant to present a heroic figure. A magical Negro is a plot device, Maleva is as much a character in the story with her own goals and values as Larry Talbot or sir John. Like Charlie Chan, Maleva represents a past period's attack on racism that was packaged to sell in the Hollywood context and slip out past the Production code which forbade showing non-whites and racial minorities of any type as equals. The compromises required to make the attack on racism makes those who fought racism look racist. Are Maria Ouspenskaya and the film where she played Maleva to be scorned because they fought to subvert a racist production code that no longer exists?<br /> <br /> As to the larger question. The Rom have been in Gothick fiction for centuries. As a widely misunderstood minority that is likely to get depicted in the kind of fiction we play with, they deserve a respectful book that deals with among other things, why they get dragged into this kind of fiction.<br /> <br /> But banishing Maleva and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esmeralda_(The_Hunchback_of_Notre-Dame)\" target=\"_blank\"> Esmeralda</a> is pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-26-2017, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:07:40-07:00","id":1115369,"title":"","content":"I know this is an older thread and got very off topic, but I wanted to briefly chime in. My father was good friends with a Cherokee medicine man and I spent a lot of my childhood visiting his home and the Cherokee reservation in western North Carolina. I love the idea of the Nunnehi and think they have just as much of a place in Changeling as the Uktena and Wendigo in Werewolf. I know that the book would have to walk a fine line between respecting the culture and keeping a fictional fairy setting. But I definitely believe it could be done. In fact, I think a Nunnehi book is desperately needed in the game line. One of the things that always bothered me (and which is still true in C20) is the very limited selection of Native American fae. There is about one per geographic region, and not even one per real-world tribe. The mythology of the tribes is extensive and rich, and as with the European fae you can see many common elements that would allow combining of fae into one &quot;kith&quot; across different tribes. I've used the Nunnehi in several games and have felt limited because I didn't have the time to do tons of research and creations of new splats. I would use them more if there was an official book for it. Get the right writers, involve true Native American historians and folklore specialists, and you can have a book that fits well with the game but still respects the heritage and culture of the people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T00:23:46-07:00","id":1115415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=862668#post862668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the bashing of Chakotay on Voyager.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I resent that!<br /> Chakotay gets bashed because his character was terribly written by stupid writers! He was supposed to be a guerilla fighter who taught advanced tactics and warfare at Starfleet Academy and then they have him spout some hippie Kumbaya-shit because he is native. The man sent a several-giga-ton nuclear warhead toward Kardassia to defend his home and then he says shit like &quot;Home is wherever you happen to be!&quot;<br /> Fuck Voyager! <br /> Sorry, some white fog clouded my mind... where were we? <br /> Honestly, WW should probably hire some consultants before writing books about cultures they don't know or understand. If not out of respect, than at least out of self-respect. I'm Austrian, I have the original &quot;A World of Darkness&quot; setting guide from 2nd Ed and when I want my entire group to pee themselves laughing, I read them the entry it has on Austria. Seriously, Shepert is right, those things need consultants, naive co-authors and the like. Otherwise we might get another *shudder* Voyager","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T17:48:01-07:00","id":1115730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=1115415#post1115415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, WW should probably hire some consultants before writing books about cultures they don't know or understand. If not out of respect, than at least out of self-respect. I'm Austrian, I have the original &quot;A World of Darkness&quot; setting guide from 2nd Ed and when I want my entire group to pee themselves laughing, I read them the entry it has on Austria. Seriously, Shepert is right, those things need consultants, naive co-authors and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! For my own games I'll do some internet searches, especially Wikipedia, if I want some background information on a place or culture. But that is not the same as being truly familiar with the original source. I might be able to run a game in Chicago by looking at travel guides and maps, but that's never going to be the same as a game run by someone who grew up and lives there. Same with various cultures. A good game company should really get experts in an area to double-check the material before publishing it if they want to have a semblance of realism in the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T09:37:12-07:00","id":1552833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook#post862643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Howdy folks, I want to include some fey types in my historical setting; the European littlefolk don't really have the right flavor, but I can't find much of anything on the native North American changelings. Any and all help would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>They seriously need to print a <b>Nunnihe </b>source book. Other non-kithian fae need source books too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T03:19:34-07:00","id":1552848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=1115415#post1115415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I resent that!<br /> Chakotay gets bashed because his character was terribly written by stupid writers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Always a problem when dealing with another cultural group. And Daveknd;n also mentioned that Chakotay gets burdened with New Agey twaddle that's and failed attempt to represent the insights of a different culture. Again a serious threat to a Nunnihe book. <br /> <br /> But just because a decent book on the Nunnihe would be very difficult doesn't mean it wouldn't be very worthwhile. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T22:11:39-07:00","id":1552866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=1552848#post1552848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But just because a decent book on the Nunnihe would be very difficult doesn't mean it wouldn't be very worthwhile.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The challenge on making a good sourcebook for the Nunnehi or any other &quot;non-kithain&quot;/&quot;culturally specific&quot; (or almost) fae is to find enough native writers.<br /> <br /> It isn't insurmountable, but generally speaking you'll want for important people in your creative team to be members of the cultures being explored, preferably members from many of them (as it's rarely a single ethnic groups being affected, even when most people outside can't tell the difference).<br /> <br /> A good amount of research, contact with the groups in question and really competent and adequately empowered cultural consultant make a huge difference and may substitute for actual writers being from the group, but it's still hard to do and not the ideal arrangement. Actually, the ideal arrangement is to have it all.<br /> <br /> Not impossible. CtD 20th Anniversary core actually did it. But for a whole sourcebook the bar is even higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T03:38:03-07:00","id":1552877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=1552866#post1552866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The challenge on making a good sourcebook for the Nunnehi or any other &quot;non-kithain&quot;/&quot;culturally specific&quot; (or almost) fae is to find enough native writers.<br /> <br /> It isn't insurmountable, but generally speaking you'll want for important people in your creative team to be members of the cultures being explored, preferably members from many of them (as it's rarely a single ethnic groups being affected, even when most people outside can't tell the difference).<br /> <br /> A good amount of research, contact with the groups in question and really competent and adequately empowered cultural consultant make a huge difference and may substitute for actual writers being from the group, but it's still hard to do and not the ideal arrangement. Actually, the ideal arrangement is to have it all.<br /> <br /> Not impossible. CtD 20th Anniversary core actually did it. But for a whole sourcebook the bar is even higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly agreed. Sympathetic and knowledgeable non members of the societies in question would be allowable too. Understanding isn't genetic trait.<br /> <br /> We must remember these are culturally sensitive gamebooks not doctrinal thesis proposals. They're supposed to be fun.<br /> <br /> And let's not forget the value of inclusion. I remember reading something written by a young black woman about the book <i>Lavender Green Magic.</i> She knew the author (Andre Norton) wasn't black, but, at a time when she was considering suicide, having someone write a book about a middle class educated black family in a respectful tone, showed her that people, even those that didn't know her, cared.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's more important to hold the door wide. Welcome is valuable in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T19:34:00-07:00","id":1552900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/862643-nunnehi-sourcebook?p=1552877#post1552877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sympathetic and knowledgeable non members of the societies in question would be allowable too.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my 3rd paragraph was essentially about that.<br /> <br /> You're right that being sympathetic may suffice. What it can't is to be counted on as a reliable strategy.<br /> <br /> More sympathetic people <i><b>think</b></i> they are knowledgeable about the groups than <i><b>actually are</b></i>. This isn't a given, but is an ever present risk.<br /> <br /> So, to minimize the risk and improve quality, you follow the advice on my 3rd paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}